  "reason": null,
  "transcript": "I believe the frontier of AI should be paced. First, safety research needs time to catch up, because right now we can build systems faster than we can test them. For example, um, labs have released models and only later discovered serious flaws. Second, pacing protects ordinary people. Imagine a nurse or a truck driver who wakes up one morning and finds that their job has disappeared overnight. Our families deserve time to adapt. Third, trust matters. A recent survey found that most people, uh, do not trust companies to regulate themselves, which means moving slower is how we earn that trust. Some people argue that slowing down lets our rivals win the race. However, a race with no brakes does not have a winner, it just has a crash. So, I think we should, you know, set the pace together. In conclusion, we should pace the frontier, because the future is worth getting right.",
